<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23978" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">instĭta</span></b> , ae, f.
		insisto. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The border</i> or <i>flounce</i>
			(laid in several plaits) <i>of a Roman lady</i>'<i>s tunic</i> (<b>poet.</b> and in
			post-Aug. prose): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quarum subsutā talos tegit instita
					veste,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 1, 2, 29</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">longa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. Am.
					1, 32</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nulla,</span>”
				i. e. <i>no lady</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 2, 600</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A bandage</i>, <i>girth</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Petr. 20</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">id. 97, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Scrib.
				Larg. 133</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 7, 654</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>